    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$512$ and $1\\,953\\,125$ ($2^9$ and $5^9$). Separate the factors of 2 and 5 so neither number ends in zero.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}1\\,000\\,000\\,000 &= 10^9\\\\&= (2\\times5)^9\\\\&= 2^9\\times5^9\\\\2^9 &= 512\\\\5^9 &= 1\\,953\\,125\\\\512\\times1\\,953\\,125 &= 1\\,000\\,000\\,000\\end{align*}$$\nA number ending in zero has both 2 and 5 as factors. Put all the factors of 2 in one number and all the factors of 5 in the other. The numbers are $512$ and $1\\,953\\,125$, and neither ends in zero.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
